---
title: Rate limits in the API
navigationTitle: Rate limits
description: General information about rate limits in the Buttondown API.
---

Buttondown enforces two types of rate limits:

| Endpoint | Rate limit |
|----------|-----------|
| All API endpoints | 600 requests per minute |
| [`POST /v1/subscribers`](/api-subscribers-create) | 100 requests per day |

If you find yourself running into the limit of 100 subscribers a day, it's likely due to one of two things:

1. You are onboarding and performing an import one subscriber at a time. We'd encourage you to use the [import path](/api-imports-create) instead to upload multiple subscribers in bulk.
2. You have a particularly high-volume list that is growing rapidly.

## Rate limit headers

Buttondown returns rate limit information in the response headers on every API request:

| Header | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| `X-RateLimit-Limit` | The maximum number of requests allowed in the current window |
| `X-RateLimit-Remaining` | The number of requests remaining in the current window |
| `X-RateLimit-Reset` | Unix timestamp (in seconds) when the rate limit window resets |

Here's an example of the headers you might see:

{% generatedMultilanguageSnippets method="GET" endpoint="/subscribers" %}
```http {% highlight="2-4" %}
HTTP/1.1 200 OK
X-RateLimit-Limit: 600
X-RateLimit-Remaining: 595
X-RateLimit-Reset: 1735776060
```
{% /generatedMultilanguageSnippets %}

## Exceeding the rate limit

If you exceed the rate limit, the API will return a `429` status code with a `Retry-After` header indicating how many seconds to wait before retrying:

{% generatedMultilanguageSnippets method="GET" endpoint="/subscribers" %}
```http {% highlight="1-2" %}
HTTP/1.1 429 Too Many Requests
Retry-After: 45
X-RateLimit-Limit: 600
X-RateLimit-Remaining: 0
X-RateLimit-Reset: 1735776060
```
{% /generatedMultilanguageSnippets %}

You can use these headers to implement backoff logic in your client code.

The daily subscriber-creation limit behaves differently: instead of a `429`, it returns a `400` whose body points you to [`POST /v1/imports`](/api-imports-create) as the supported way to add subscribers in bulk.
